## Spec
`framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/05-location-relocation/05-host-relocation-flow.ko.md` §14 step 2:
"`Draining` descriptor를 게시해 새 selection과 placement에서 제외한다. 게시의 terminal(성공 또는 실패)만 기다리며,
게시 뒤 전파를 위한 시간 대기는 두지 않는다." Step 6 defines the bounded outcomes (`Stopped/None`,
`ForceStopped/DeadlineExceeded`, `ForceStopped/TeardownFailed`).

## Cause (verified by the supervisor, D-106)
`framework/languages/dotnet/src/Zlink.Framework/Runtime/Host/ZLinkFrameworkDrainExecutor.cs`:
`PublishDrainingMarkerAsync` loops: a `false` from `MarkDraining` or any exception is swallowed, then
`Task.Delay(_locationOptions.PollingInterval)` and the same publication is resubmitted until the deadline token
cancels. `PublishServingWeightAsync` (`QuiesceServingChannels` false → delay → retry) and `CleanupOwnerAsync`
(exception → delay → retry) have the same shape. These are the timed-wait/resubmit mitigations §14 forbids; they
burn the shutdown deadline before `wait_accepted_operations`. Java/Kotlin and Node consume the first terminal.

## What to do
Each of the three steps consumes the first terminal of its operation exactly once: success → next step;
failure (false or exception) → the existing result path (`DrainingStatePublishFailed` for the two publications;
the existing teardown-failure result for owner cleanup), recorded in the failure list the executor already keeps.
Remove the `while (true)` + `Task.Delay` loops; add no new state. Regression tests: (1) a store whose
`MarkDraining` fails once ends shutdown with `DrainingStatePublishFailed` without waiting `PollingInterval`
(assert elapsed < PollingInterval using a monotonic clock/`TimeProvider`); (2) success path unchanged; (3) owner
cleanup failure → existing teardown-failed result, no retry. Check `ZoneWorld`/`ShoppingMall` sample expectations
that might have relied on the retry (search tests for `DrainingStatePublishFailed`).

